---
import '../styles/kit.css';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Badge from '../components/Badge.astro';
import { href, GITHUB_URL } from '../lib/site';

---

<Page path="/about">
	<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
	    <div class="bd first"><div class="wrap"><h1 class="t60">Why a11ign exists</h1></div></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-label="Why we built it"><p class="statement">Most accessibility checks read your code. We listen to your page.</p></section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="gap"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="gap" class="t36">The gap we saw</h2></div>
<div class="duo"><div><div class="bignum"><span>57%</span></div><p class="bigcap">of WCAG issues are found automatically by axe-core, according to Deque.</p></div><div><p>Automated checks read your code. <span class="hl">They can’t hear your page.</span> The rest is left for a person to review, and much of it is what it’s really like to use a screen reader.</p><p>Testing with a real screen reader is the answer, but it’s slow, Windows-only and hard to repeat, so most teams skip it. We built a11ign to change that: real NVDA, on a machine GitHub provides, with the proof quoted on your pull request.</p></div></div>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="hear"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="hear" class="t36">Hear the difference</h2></div>
<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">Same page, two versions. The only change is one missing image description. This is what real NVDA said.</p><div class="tpw"><div class="tp"><div class="th"><span>Accessible version</span><span>What NVDA said</span></div><div class="ln"><b>1.</b><span>heading, level 1, Project update</span></div><div class="ln"><b>2.</b><span>The garden project added a shaded seating area.</span></div><div class="ln ok"><b>3.</b><span>graphic, A shaded seating area beside the community garden</span></div></div><div class="tp"><div class="th"><span>Broken version</span><span>What NVDA said</span></div><div class="ln"><b>1.</b><span>heading, level 1, Project update</span></div><div class="ln"><b>2.</b><span>The garden project added a shaded seating area.</span></div><div class="ln bad"><b>3.</b><span>graphic, To get missing image descriptions, open the context menu.</span></div></div></div><p class="muted">A real pair from our test pages.</p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="beliefs"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="beliefs" class="t36">What we believe</h2></div>
<ul class="rows"><li><h3>Proof, not scores</h3><p>Every finding quotes what the screen reader said. There’s no score or badge, because one number hides what was not checked.</p></li><li><h3>Clear scope first</h3><p>We say what a11ign covers, and what’s still to come, up front.</p></li><li><h3>No data sent to us</h3><p>We never see your code, and there’s no tracking or phoning home. If that ever changes, it will be opt-in and arrive in a major version.</p></li><li><h3>Open by licence</h3><p>Licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later. Anyone who runs a modified version as a service has to share their changes.</p></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="built"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="built" class="t36">How it’s built</h2></div>
<ul class="rows"><li><h3>A testing pipeline</h3><p>Drives real NVDA through a page, checks what it said, and reports findings against WCAG.</p></li><li><h3>Repeatable setup</h3><p>A scripted Windows build and GitHub-hosted runners mean anyone can run it, the same way each time.</p></li><li><h3>Our own model</h3><p>Trained on what the first two produce. It flags findings for a person to judge. It doesn’t decide them.</p></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="who"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="who" class="t36">Who’s behind it</h2></div>
<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">a11ign is the work of Daniel Beck, who built it. Charlotte Williams leads the product.</p><ul class="grid team">
	<li class="person"><div class="av" aria-hidden="true">DB</div><div><h3 class="t22">Daniel Beck</h3><p class="muted">Founder</p><p class="muted">The brains behind a11ign.</p><p><a class="lnk2 solo" href="https://danielbeck.dev/">danielbeck.dev</a></p></div></li>
	<li class="person"><div class="av" aria-hidden="true">CW</div><div><h3 class="t22">Charlotte Williams</h3><p class="muted">Product Manager</p></div></li>
	</ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd alt"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="next"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="next" class="t36">Where we’re going</h2></div>
<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">a11ign is live and working today. Here’s what we’re building next.</p><ul class="grid"><li><div class="rm"><Badge>Coming soon</Badge><h3>A screen reader’s view on every commit</h3><p>A quick check that runs inside the Playwright tests you already have. No Windows machine and no extra pipeline.</p></div></li><li><div class="rm"><Badge>Planned</Badge><h3>More screen readers</h3><p>Test with the ones your users actually use. JAWS and VoiceOver are next, then Orca.</p></div></li><li><div class="rm"><Badge>Planned</Badge><h3>Whole journeys, not just pages</h3><p>Sign up, search, check out. Playwright drives the page while the screen reader listens to every step.</p></div></li><li><div class="rm"><Badge>Planned</Badge><h3>Catch the wrong voice</h3><p>Hear when a page is read out in the wrong language, or when a button’s announced name doesn’t match what’s on screen.</p></div></li></ul><p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">Star the project to follow along as each one lands.</p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="join"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="join" class="t36">Run it, review it, or help build it</h2></div>
<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">We want your honest reaction more than praise. If you’re an accessibility specialist, we would love your review too.</p><div class="ctaRow"><Button size="lg" href={href('/get-started')}>Add to your workflow</Button><Button size="lg" variant="secondary" icon="github" href={GITHUB_URL}>Star on GitHub</Button></div>
	    </section></div>
	  </main>
</Page>
